# Example 16: an active-site zoom.
# The HNH nuclease site of SpCas9 in the catalytic state, PDB 7Z4J
# (Pacesa et al. 2022, Nature 609:191). One Mg2+ is held by D839 and
# N863 and by the scissile phosphate of the cleaved target strand, with
# waters completing the coordination shell.
#
# This is the tightest panel class in the stylebook and it follows
# different rules from an overview:
#
#   hide everything that is not the site. Not faded, hidden. At this zoom
#   a ribbon two shells away is noise that costs contrast.
#   sticks get heteroatom coloring: carbon takes the domain color, and
#   oxygen, nitrogen and phosphorus keep element colors. That is the one
#   place the house palette yields, because a reader identifies atoms by
#   red and blue faster than by any scheme we could invent.
#   the backbone cartoon goes pale and thick so it reads as a container
#   rather than competing with the sticks.
#   coordination and hydrogen bonds are dashed, thin, and a single muted
#   color that is in neither the element palette nor the domain palette,
#   so a dash is never mistaken for an atom or a domain.
#   labels are plain text on the atom, no box and no leader line. At this
#   magnification there is room to place them, and a chip with a leader
#   would out-weigh the chemistry it points at.
#   silhouettes stay on. They are what separates the foreground sticks
#   from the backbone behind them.
open 7z4j
open ../../palettes/lab_colors.cxc
open ../../presets/Base/publication_white.cxc

# Strip the scene back to nothing, then add only the site. The base
# preset turns on every nucleic-acid atom so that ladders and slabs draw,
# which is right for an overview and is exactly the clutter that ruins a
# zoom: two whole duplexes end up in frame edge to edge.
hide #1 atoms
hide #1 cartoons
~nucleotides

# One metal, the one in the HNH site. The entry has four, and the others
# belong to RuvC and to the sgRNA fold.
show (:MG & /B:1403) atoms
show (:HOH & (:MG & /B:1403) :<3.0) atoms

# Backbone only within one shell of the metal
show (:MG & /B:1403) :<9 cartoons

# Backbone neutral and pale, so it reads as a container. Do not give the
# cartoon the same hue as the sticks in front of it, however tempting the
# domain colour is: at this zoom the sticks stop being findable.
color #1 lab_gray_p
cartoon style xsection oval width 0.8 thickness 0.22

# The site: HNH catalytic residues, the cleaved target strand ends,
# and the metal
show /B:839,840,863 atoms
style /B:839,840,863 stick
show /c:3 atoms
show /C:4 atoms
style (/c:3 | /C:4) stick
nucleotides (/c:3 | /C:4) atoms

# Heteroatom coloring: carbons take the domain color, elements keep theirs
color /B:839,840,863 lab_hnh target a
color /c:3 lab_target target a
color /C:4 lab_target target a
color (/B:839,840,863 | /c:3 | /C:4) & N cornflower blue target a
color (/B:839,840,863 | /c:3 | /C:4) & O firebrick target a
color (/B:839,840,863 | /c:3 | /C:4) & P goldenrod target a

# Metal and waters as spheres, sized so the metal reads as the centre
style :MG sphere
size :MG atomRadius 1.1
color :MG lab_purple
style :HOH sphere
size :HOH atomRadius 0.45
color :HOH firebrick

size stickRadius 0.22

# Coordination and hydrogen bonds. A single muted colour, thin, dashed.
#
# Do not write a bare "show pseudobonds" here. That turns on every
# pseudobond group in the model, including missing-structure dashes,
# which at this zoom scatter little specks across the whole panel. Show
# only the pseudobonds that touch the metal.
show (:MG & /B:1403) target p
color (:MG & /B:1403) #8A7FB5 target p
size pseudobondRadius 0.08
hbonds /B:839,840,863 restrict (/c:3 | /C:4) reveal false color #8A7FB5 radius 0.08 dashes 8 showDist false

# Plain labels on the atom, no box, no leader
# Offsets are in Angstrom along the screen axes. Nudge each one by hand
# until nothing collides; there is no automatic placement.
label /B:839 residues text "{0.name} {0.number}" height 0.85 color black offset 2.6,-2.6,0
label /B:840 residues text "{0.name} {0.number}" height 0.85 color black offset -7.5,2.2,0
label /B:863 residues text "{0.name} {0.number}" height 0.85 color black offset 2.4,-5.4,0
label /B:1403 residues text "Mg2+" height 0.95 color black offset -1.2,2.6,0

# Frame on the site as a whole, not on the single metal atom. Framing on
# one atom and then padding out is how you end up with a wide shot of
# nothing; give view the residues you actually want in the panel.
#
# Orientation was chosen by rendering a ring of candidates and looking at
# them, not guessed. scripts/orbit.sh does that sweep for you. Rotate
# first and frame second: view changes zoom and centre but not
# orientation, so a turn after it will swing the site back out of frame.
windowsize 1000 900
cofr (:MG & /B:1403)
turn y 80
turn x 25
view (/B:839,840,863 | /c:3 | /C:4 | (:MG & /B:1403)) pad 0.55

2dlabels text "HNH active site" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.95 size 22 color lab_black bold true
2dlabels text "7Z4J  catalytic state" xpos 0.03 ypos 0.03 size 17 color lab_gray

save active_site.png width 2600 supersample 3
